course: dictionary
lesson: 14433
title: A new science word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are new, but their parts can give you clues. Oxygen is a gas we breathe. The ending -ate turns a word into a verb, an action. So to oxygenate something means to put oxygen into it.
explain: «The lungs oxygenate the blood.» The lungs take oxygen from the air and put it into the blood. The sentence tells you the action, and the word oxygen in the middle helps you guess what the action is.
explain: «Pond plants oxygenate the water, so the fish can breathe.» Here the water gets oxygen from the plants. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Pond plants add oxygen to the water, so the fish can breathe." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: To oxygenate means to add oxygen to something, such as water or blood.
fact: «Oxygenated» is an adjective that means containing oxygen, as in «oxygenated blood».
fact: «Oxygenated blood» goes from the heart to the body.
fact: «Air pumps» and «pond plants» can oxygenate water for fish.
fact: Waterfalls and waves can also oxygenate rivers and seas, which helps the creatures in them.
exercise: «Pond plants oxygenate the water for the fish.» What does oxygenate mean here? | Fill with sand | Take oxygen away from | *Add oxygen to | Heat up
exercise: Which word in «Oxygenated blood is bright red» tells you the blood contains oxygen? | red | blood | *Oxygenated | bright
exercise: Which part of the body does the job in «The lungs oxygenate the blood»? | Heart | Skin | *Lungs | Stomach
test: «Air pumps help to oxygenate the water in the tank.» What does oxygenate mean? | Make the water cold | Make the water salty | *Add oxygen to the water | Remove the water
test: Which word describes blood that contains oxygen? | Oxygenate | *Oxygenated | Oxygen-free | Blood-red
exam: «The fish were happy because the plants oxygenate the pond.» What does oxygenate mean? | *Add oxygen to the pond | Empty the pond | Freeze the pond | Fill with mud
